3:When the blazing heat of August has only just passed is the best time to climb mountains. The foothills are covered with people who seem to have had just the same idea as me.
6:Two people nearby are staring at the man by my side as if seeing something incredible while muttering something in low voices. This seems to remind other passers-by, who also stop to watch. Some even fish out cameras and begin taking pictures.
7:He hasn't done anything special to attract attention, and is only—like many others—warming up in preparation for climbing the mountain. But I have to say if there's one thing that can attract so much attention, of course, it's definitely his phenomenal physique.
8:Biceps bulging like logs; sturdy pecs against which his shirt lay taut; a broad, strong and reassuring back; quads whose powerful curves could still be seen even under his loose clothing; and those calves that supported his nimble fleet.
9:Strong but not intimidating, his natural, healthy physique makes him look far younger than his actual age, and full of vigor. He's just standing there, yet still manages to give everyone the impression of a classical sculpture. Onlookers can't help but gasp in admiration: Such a strong and powerful man! So strong, so powerful!
14:Many people present may share the same doubts and sentiments. After all, in the public perception, jungles, glaciers, and other remote, dangerous places seem to be more fitting for this explorer.
15:But he really is only here to climb the mountain. We'd been chatting a few days ago, and he had invited me along for a workout...
24:It's just exercise, no need to put your life on the line...
30:Sorry, Joseph. It's not the weather making me so tired. I just haven't been getting enough sleep.
31:But what am I supposed to do... Elderian Ring is just too addictive!
32:I'd barely slept all week because of the newly released game. If he hadn't called me in the morning, I would have completely forgotten all about our plan to go climbing.
35:I splash some water on my face after warming up, and immediately feel a lot more awake. Joseph had rushed over to meet me right after a shoot, so it's a little rude of me to look so out of it while talking to him.
36:Besides, I'm not the only one that didn't have enough sleep. I'm sure I'll be just as perky as him, once we get going.
39:Totally not what I expected... It isn't long before I'm puffing and panting away. Forget about being perky... I'm even feeling a little dizzy.
41:Joseph, in the lead, is still in fine spirits. So fine, in fact, that he's playing some kind of echo game with the mountains.
42:I was too naive... We are simply not on the same level. He can walk for almost a full day without a rest. I can't believe I actually thought I'd be as energetic as he is.
45:This is awkward. I check the time and cannot believe we've only been going for twenty minutes... Is it too soon to ask for a break?
48:In that case...
53:Joseph seems to have consciously slowed down, most likely out of consideration for me.
54:It's not often there's a chance to get out and relax like this. Best not to spoil it by making him worry too much.
58:Who would have thought it'd be this tiring to... climb a mountain? I hang on and walk a bit more, and the cool breeze seems to have a soporific effect.
60:Joseph keeps increasing his pace... No, that's not right. It's me who's getting slower and slower. I need to pick it up! I'm already lagging, and who's to say he won't just have vanished by the next time I blink?
61:Easy enough to think that, but honestly I'm already going as fast as I can. And my anxiety isn't helping me walk any quicker, but is weighing me down even more.
65:Is... Is this what he meant by "not too much longer"?! Well, I guess from Joseph's point of view this brief period is nothing. I was careless... I should have asked.
67:Walking another hour in my current state is no joke...
76:As daylight slowly fades, the scene in front of me gradually warps into nothing but a blur. The refreshing coolness of the evening air permeates every limb, giving me the feeling of being immersed in seawater.
78:I look down at my hands, but can't even see them.
80:...
82:By the time I regain consciousness, the surrounding scene is plated in the muted colors of dusk.
90:I've seen him princess-carrying his colleagues back to camp in the show, but thank my lucky stars he didn't do that with me. Fainting while walking up a mountain is bad enough—if he had to carry me back down like that, I'd have to go live in a different city.
97:I love listening to Joseph's travel stories whenever we eat together. I don't know what wonders he'll talk about this time, but I bet they're worth looking forward to!
101:I remember I brought some jerky snacks, so I take some out and feed him... Huh? There's something hard sliding around by my ear? It's not a bug, is it?!
102:I gingerly reach out an exploratory hand, only to find that George was rubbing something in his mouth against my ear. I take the object from him, and find a round, blue stone.
108:While it is a beautiful stone, it isn't a sapphire like he had claimed. If I can pick up something as lovely as this just by climbing a mountain, I should probably go buy a couple of lottery tickets. But it's always nice to receive a present, and it deserves a good meal.
114:The photo of the gemstone displayed on the screen seems familiar, and I can't help but glance at the "stone" that I'd stuck to the bedside.
116:I should get Nikaidou to properly appraise this for me, just in case, you know? I certainly don't want to cause any diplomatic trouble.
117:...While I'm at it, should I go buy that lottery ticket?
119:I have to admit it is a little embarrassing to ask for a rest after such a short distance, but it is what it is. Leisure time is meant to be enjoyed, so breaks are fine whenever one is needed.
120:We found a roadside stall and sat down, ordering something to eat while we watch the world go by.
127:Chatting with Joseph always makes me happy. His straightforward manner relieves a lot of my guilt.
135:This conversation makes me want to skip the game with Kazuha Saionji the day after tomorrow.
147:Although I took several more breaks along the way, we actually manage to reach the summit by noon as planned.
151:Without any suitable comparison at present, I will reserve judgment about it being the "best" viewing area. But there's no denying it's one of the best places to see the city sights.
152:From the lofty vantage point, the city seems to have become an exquisite model—this is definitely a new experience! When I think how, not long ago, I was a part of this "model" too, a sense of wonder is added to the refreshing feeling.
161:Joseph stays silent for a moment, before smiling and patting my shoulder.
166:Joseph bends over and picks up a blue stone from the ground, his palm shining in the sun.
169:One could say I've learned a lesson today. If you can treat every journey like he does, then maybe there'd never be a moment of boredom.
170:Just being around him automatically lifts my spirits, no matter how exhausted I am. People like him, who know how to enjoy life, can always affect those around them with their vitality and energy.
175:Although it is a little cheeky, Joseph is clearly offering me a way out. I'd be an idiot to refuse.
179:By the time we walk down the mountain, lights have already been lit up all over the street. We find a cozy little restaurant and celebrate the conclusion of today's journey with a delicious meal.
182:Returning home, I place the "sapphire" carefully in a drawer, wondering when I can find a chain to hang it on as a souvenir of today...
184:But I never expected fate to only allow me to have it for one night...
187:I look closely at the images on the screen, positive that I've seen something similar only recently...
188:Just as I'm about to pull the object out of the drawer for comparison, the phone rings.
191:I can't keep this... This might cause a serious diplomatic problem.
192:Huff... The weather's nice.
193:{character:Tourist A} Hey, look! Isn't that...
194:{character:Tourist B} Huh? Oh?! It really is him...
195:{character:Joseph} Alright! Warm up, check!
196:{character:Tourist A} Is he here to climb too? Never thought he would be interested in such an ordinary mountain.
197:{character:Tourist B} Is he doing a show? Otherwise why would he come here? This mountain is way too easy for him.
198:{character:player} ...Neck hurts. Back hurts. Playing back-to-back Hanchan games has made me feel pretty bad.
199:{character:Nana Shiraishi} You're clearly not getting enough exercise, junior. Oh, I won with this tile, hee-hee.
200:{character:player} Ah, I was busy complaining and didn't even notice that 4 Han with rounded up Fu scores. Ouch.
202:{character:player} Mountain climbing...? I haven't been doing that for such a long time that it actually sounds like a great idea. But just to be sure, you do mean ordinary walking up the mountain, right? Not one of those extreme challenges like on your show?
203:{character:Joseph} If you're interested in that, my friend, then we can always find a more unusual route to the summit!
204:{character:player} No, no! No need! Thank you! Just a normal path is fine.
205:{character:Joseph} Finished your warm-up, friend?
206:{character:player} More or less. Let's go... *Yawn*
207:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! It's a nice breeze, but it makes people sleepy.
208:{character:player} Th-that's for sure, haha...
211:{character:player} Huff... Ah... Huff...
212:{character:Joseph} How... Are... You...?!
213:{character:Joseph} What say you to a break, friend?
214:{character:player} Ye-yeah! We've been going a while, and I'm already a little tired...
215:{character:player} If we keep going at this pace, how long do you think it'll be until we make it to the summit, Joseph?
216:{character:Joseph} At this pace? I reckon... Probably not too much longer.
217:Keep going a while longer
