228:{character:Joseph} Hahah! It takes a strong body to play Mahjong. Seeing as we have some good weather, why don't we get some exercise and go climb a mountain?
229:{character:player} How about we rest a little bit later?
230:{character:Joseph} Are you okay, my friend? I hope I'm just being oversensitive, but you don't look too great.
231:{character:player} I'm fine, really. It's probably because I'm not used to mountain climbing. It's been ages since the last time I went.
232:{character:player} Don't worry. I'm not so weak that I can't handle this little bit of hiking. I'll be fine if I go a bit slower.
233:{character:Joseph} ...Alright. Don't push yourself too hard, my friend. Remember we're here to have fun!
234:{character:Joseph} Hum hmm hum! ♪
235:{character:player} I feel like we've been walking for miles, Joseph. How long till we get to the top?
236:{character:Joseph} Let me see... We've been going about 40 minutes already, so I'd say about another hour or so.
237:{character:player} An, an hour?!
238:{character:player} Stop, hold up a second!
239:{character:Joseph} Huh? Oh... Sorry. I'm walking too fast, aren't I? I can't seem to fix this bad habit. The crew of the show always complain about this, saying that one minute I was there, and the next I was already gone.
240:{character:player} It's fine, I just think it might be time to rest...
241:{character:Joseph} Don't be in a hurry to sit down, and don't be gulping down water just yet. First, you need to adjust your breathing.
242:{character:Joseph} Slow, deep breaths. Try to keep them even. Here, you can use this towel to wipe your face. Wow... Your sweat just keeps coming! Are you sure you're alright?
243:{character:player} Yeah, I think so. Huff... Adjust breathing... In and out...
244:{character:player} ...I think I'm alright. At least I'm not panting so heavily anymore. Uh, Joseph—is it going to rain?
245:{character:Joseph} Rain? It's a fine, sunny day right now, my friend.
246:{character:player} How odd... Why's it getting dark?
247:{character:player} Who turned out the lights...?
248:{character:Joseph} Did you sleep well?
249:{character:player} So well! Definitely the best sleep I've had in the past few days.
250:{character:player} This is... The foot of the mountain where we started?
251:{character:Joseph} Yep. You just conked out, scaring me half to death, hahaha! You didn't wake up for so long that I brought you here, where you could get better rest.
252:{character:player} Thank you... But I have to ask, how did you carry me down the mountain?
253:{character:Joseph} On my back. Why?
254:{character:player} It's nothing. Just curious.
255:{character:Joseph} Don't you feel better after a good rest?
256:{character:player} Well, yeah! Definitely more alert, but also starving. If I ate a good meal, I'm sure I could easily run up and down this mountain—twice!
257:{character:player} Although, it's not the best time to climb now... I'm sorry, Joseph. Let me take you for dinner tonight, as it was my fault we didn't make it to the top.
258:{character:Joseph} Don't say that, my friend. It's my fault for not realizing you were in trouble sooner. Allow me to take you for dinner instead.
259:{character:Joseph} All journeys have a few small hiccups. We'll have plenty of chances to come here again, so let's not allow a small setback to affect our future enjoyment.
260:{character:player} All this talk of dinner is making me even hungrier! Okay, let's have a really good meal, and eat away our regret of not making it to the top!
261:{character:George} Screech, screeech!
262:{character:Joseph} If this little guy's rubbing your face, it must be because he wants to cheer you up too.
263:{character:player} Yeah? Well, thanks for the comfort, George.
264:{character:Joseph} He even brought you a gift, a beautiful sapphire! Hey, buddy, how come you never comfort me like this?
265:{character:player} Maybe it's because I sneaked him snacks! Such an elegant gift deserves one in return. So, George, this whole pack of jerky is yours.
266:{character:George} Screeeech!
267:{character:Joseph} Even though we didn't make it to the top, finding such a wonderful little treasure is surely worth celebrating!
268:{character:player} Then let us celebrate! What do you fancy eating? Your choice.
269:{character:News Anchor} We interrupt your program to bring you breaking news: During a recent visit to our city, a member of the E Kingdom royal family accidentally lost the gemstone from their ring...
270:{character:player} How unlucky! Losing something so precious on so rare a trip. Erm, this place does great bagels!
271:{character:News Anchor} The lost sapphire has not, at present, been recovered. We ask anyone who finds such an item to contact us as soon as possible.
272:{character:player} Sapphire... Huh?!
273:{character:player} No way! Surely that's too far a coincidence, right?
