280:{character:player} ...I'll listen to you then. Let's find a place to sit.
281:{character:player} So cold! Has this just thawed...? But at least it woke me right up.
282:{character:Joseph} Cool. Did you not sleep well last night?
283:{character:player} I've been up late these past few days playing a new game. I'm sorry, you invite me out and I turn up with dark circles under my eyes...
284:{character:Joseph} Don't worry about it. It's hard enough to find something that really grabs you like that, so why not enjoy it while you do? That is called living.
285:{character:Joseph} The very fact that you are willing to leave your game and come with me here shows that you value our friendship. And that makes me happy. So there's no reason at all to apologize! Smile instead, my friend.
286:{character:player} Alright! Treat it like I hadn't properly woken up and was mumbling nonsense.
287:{character:Joseph} But I'm not going to lie, my friend—those are some pretty impressive dark circles, almost like you got in a fight. Be sure to have a good dinner and get some rest.
288:{character:player} Yeah, I agree. I do need a good night's sleep. That reminds me, Joseph... You came right here as soon as you finished the shoot. Aren't you tired too?
289:{character:Joseph} As long as you have good exercise habits, doing a little extra work once in a while is nothing.
290:{character:Joseph} Exercise helps with many things, including Mahjong. After all, it is a game that demands both the body AND the mind. It can never hurt to be in good physical shape.
291:{character:player} I've heard that before, from Kazuha Saionji. She has often told me that I'm not strong enough to keep up with her training.
292:{character:Joseph} Ahaha! Even I find it hard to keep up with that girl. It's tough that you have to train under her now.
293:{character:player} Whoa... If even you can't keep up, then what hope is there for me in such a short period of time?
294:{character:Joseph} Don't lose heart! If you can accomplish something in the short term, just take it as a longer-term goal and make short-term preparation for it.
295:{character:player} What sort of short-term preparations? Can you give me an example?
296:{character:Joseph} Let me see... First, how about training to walk 20 hours without stopping?
297:{character:player} Never mind...
298:{character:player} I think I've caught up on my sleep. Let's get back on the road, Joseph.
299:Again, we are just not on the same level... His "short-term goals" are probably considered "long-term goals" for most people.
300:{character:Joseph} Okay. As you wish, my friend.
301:{character:Joseph} We have reached the summit, the highest point in all of One Han City!
302:{character:player} Huh?! Isn't that Kana's advertisement? Even here...
303:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! Look at the scenery further out, friend.
305:{character:Joseph} When I flew by here in a helicopter, I thought it should be the best view in all of One Han City. And it does not disappoint me!
306:{character:player} Really? Let me see!
307:{character:player} Looking out at such a sight really makes it all worthwhile.
308:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! Most of the hard work of hiking is all for these kinds of moments. So enjoy it! Enjoy it, my friend.
309:{character:player} What about you, Joseph? Are you enjoying it too?
310:{character:Joseph} Of course! Making it to the top, conquering the summit—it's always a pleasure, no matter how many times you've done it before.
311:{character:player} As long as you're having fun. I was worried you'd be bored.
312:{character:Joseph} Bored? How so?
314:{character:player} I wasn't in the best form today, making stops the whole way like that. Fortunately you weren't disappointed.
315:{character:Joseph} I see. Well, my friend, let me ask you: What do you think is the most important thing for me before I travel or go on some adventure?
316:{character:player} Let me think... Is it being fully prepared?
317:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! That's a great answer, but even more important is the mindset. Wherever I go, I must first respect the journey.
318:{character:Joseph} Respect nature, encounters, the unexpected, surprises... Take every step with sincerity and, at least in my opinion, with this mentality you will never be bored. Also...
319:{character:Joseph} Good things always happen to you! Would you look at that! What a gorgeous sapphire. Nature loves to give us these surprises from time to time.
320:{character:player} Hahaha! For real! It's so dazzling, too.
321:{character:Joseph} This is for you, my friend.
322:{character:player} Eh? I don't know... I haven't done anything special, how could I take such a lovely gift from you?
323:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! Did you forget? You didn't get enough sleep, yet you still managed to reach the top of the mountain with me. Such perseverance deserves a reward. Good job, my friend!
324:{character:player} ...Thank you. Then I'll take it.
325:{character:Joseph} Found something interesting, buddy? George is calling us, let's go see what he wants.
326:{character:player} Let's go!
327:{character:player} I haven't sweated like that in years, but at least my back doesn't seem so sore anymore. I guess I do need to exercise more. I should hike with Joseph again someday!
328:{character:player} Urgh... Surely it's not the same gemstone, right? It would be too much of a coincidence if it is...
329:{character:Joseph} Did you see the news, my friend? I think I saw something familiar.
330:{character:player} ...Your timing is perfect. Why don't we go to Tenhoukaku later if you are free?
331:The reason for such attention is actually very simple. It's because he is Joseph, a celebrity and household name in One Han City.
333:{character:player} Perfect! Let's go, and we can think about what to have for dinner on the way.
334:{character:Joseph} Hmm, nice. Come take a look, my friend.
335:{character:player} Well, it's like what those two tourists said. Compared with your previous adventures, this mountain is way too easy for you. I worry that it won't be exciting enough for you.
336:{character:Joseph} When we reach the summit, we'll find a patch of grass and have a nap while the wind blows all around us. After we wake up, we'll walk back down the mountain to have a good meal. And then, we will have ourselves an absolutely perfect day!
